      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "On the Importance of Paralanguage",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "On the Importance of Paralanguage",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "vAMnWgszvchHWuelouU15",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2940.37471561016,
      "y": -1307.3995867195786,
      "width": 943.8391723632812,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "VwfDJJ4o20aUSFCZ2Si8v"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 893955504,
      "version": 4004,
      "versionNonce": 1782614475,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790083253320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Human communication is not solely made of pure linguistic information (words and sentences).\nSpeech is a fundamental aspect of human communication. Little is known about the timing of \nlanguage's emergence in the human species, but surely speech was one of the first means of \ncommunications. Proto-writing emerged as early as the 7th millennium BC in China, but \nbefore that oral tradition was the sole tool for passing knowledge through.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn speech, on top of linguistic information there is a paralinguistic component.\nParalanguage is a feature of human communication that may modify meaning, give nuanced \nmeaning, or convey emotion, by using suprasegmental techniques such as prosody, including pitch, \nvolume, intonation, etc.\n\n==> if we want AI to truly be integrated in our life, it has to master all the levels of human \ncommunications including paralanguage: we need communication models\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Human communication is not solely made of pure linguistic information (words and sentences).\nSpeech is a fundamental aspect of human communication. Little is known about the timing of \nlanguage's emergence in the human species, but surely speech was one of the first means of \ncommunications. Proto-writing emerged as early as the 7th millennium BC in China, but \nbefore that oral tradition was the sole tool for passing knowledge through.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn speech, on top of linguistic information there is a paralinguistic component.\nParalanguage is a feature of human communication that may modify meaning, give nuanced \nmeaning, or convey emotion, by using suprasegmental techniques such as prosody, including pitch, \nvolume, intonation, etc.\n\n==> if we want AI to truly be integrated in our life, it has to master all the levels of human \ncommunications including paralanguage: we need communication models\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
