    {
      "id": "LwWjz4BQD_-CU3rj06bzI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3239.919431713359,
      "y": 2373.4560130002646,
      "width": 1053.0389404296875,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "nUmrjycYwa2VKrbE72_7w"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b93",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 858006629,
      "version": 4361,
      "versionNonce": 111349995,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790086344441,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CSM fast overview:\n    - is a multimodal, text and speech model \n    - RVQ tokens. \n    - RQ-Transformer with two autoregressive transformers. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBoth transformers are variants of the Llama architecture (meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B). Text tokens \nare generated via a Llama  tokenizer, while audio is processed using Mimi.\n\nThe reconstructed audio token is then autoregressively fed back into the Backbone for the next step. \nThis process begins again on the next inference request, with the interim audio (such as a user utterance) \nbeing represented by interleaved audio and text transcription token.\n\nCSM is currently trained on primarily English data; some multilingual ability emerges due to dataset \ncontamination, but it does not perform well yet.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CSM fast overview:\n    - is a multimodal, text and speech model \n    - RVQ tokens. \n    - RQ-Transformer with two autoregressive transformers. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBoth transformers are variants of the Llama architecture (meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B). Text tokens \nare generated via a Llama  tokenizer, while audio is processed using Mimi.\n\nThe reconstructed audio token is then autoregressively fed back into the Backbone for the next step. \nThis process begins again on the next inference request, with the interim audio (such as a user utterance) \nbeing represented by interleaved audio and text transcription token.\n\nCSM is currently trained on primarily English data; some multilingual ability emerges due to dataset \ncontamination, but it does not perform well yet.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790085095076,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
