    {
      "id": "pBstwoYdsJwZQoTMH0pBN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3228.413130201945,
      "y": 3373.869907802211,
      "width": 1161.7388916015625,
      "height": 2600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "jM6ssg04SazYFJK8_Ey4t"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1711035621,
      "version": 4988,
      "versionNonce": 1547659371,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790086344441,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Orpheus is a family of speech-LLMs. We're also releasing a pretrained and finetuned model in 4 sizes based on \nthe Llama architecture:\n    - Medium – 3B parameters\n    - Small – 1B parameters\n    - Tiny – 400M parameters\n    - Nano – 150M parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nZero-shot cloning prerained model. While our pretrained model has not been trained on any voice \ncloning objective, zero-shot voice cloning can emerge due to the large amounts of pretraining data.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is possible to teach the base model to \nspeak with a specific emotion using a few \ndozen high quality finetuning examples. \n    --> emotion tags\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRealtime usage enables conversational use cases. Our model supports realtime output streaming with \nvery low latency of around ~ 200 ms. For even lower latency, input streaming of text into the KV cache \nof our model can reduce latencies down to ~25-50 ms.\n\nThere are two new design paradigms.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOpheuss use SNAC as (CNN-based) tokenizer.\nIn input, it gets 7 tokens per frame which are decoded as a single flattened sequence. \nThis decreases the number of steps the model is required to generate. The model is able to generate tokens \ncomfortably faster than realtime playback using a straightforward vLLM implementation on an A100 or H100 \nGPU, which means longer sequences are still generated in realtime.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSNAC utilizes a hierarchy of quantizers operating at multiple temporal resolutions, allowing the codec to capture \ndetails at different time levels more efficiently.\n\nIn standard RVQ codebook operates at that same temporal resolution. \n    --> all information — from very slow-changing semantic structure to extremely fine-grained acoustic detail — \n        must be represented at the same temporal rate.\n    --> more tokens are used to represent phenomena that change very slowly.\n\nInstead of quantizing all residuals at the same frame rate, SNAC introduces a hierarchy, where each \nquantizer operates at a different temporal resolution. \n\nAt each iteration i, they downsample the residuals using average pooling , perform codebook lookup, and then upsample \nagain with nearest-neighbor interpolation by the same factor to match the original temporal resolution.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMultilingual support! Canopy Labs also released on huggingface Orpheus Multilingual, a family of speech-LLMs, for \nmultiple languages: French, German, Spanish, Italian, Chinese, Korean, and Hindi. \nThe fine tuned versions have finite set of Voices and emotion tags.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Orpheus is a family of speech-LLMs. We're also releasing a pretrained and finetuned model in 4 sizes based on \nthe Llama architecture:\n    - Medium – 3B parameters\n    - Small – 1B parameters\n    - Tiny – 400M parameters\n    - Nano – 150M parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nZero-shot cloning prerained model. While our pretrained model has not been trained on any voice \ncloning objective, zero-shot voice cloning can emerge due to the large amounts of pretraining data.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is possible to teach the base model to \nspeak with a specific emotion using a few \ndozen high quality finetuning examples. \n    --> emotion tags\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRealtime usage enables conversational use cases. Our model supports realtime output streaming with \nvery low latency of around ~ 200 ms. For even lower latency, input streaming of text into the KV cache \nof our model can reduce latencies down to ~25-50 ms.\n\nThere are two new design paradigms.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOpheuss use SNAC as (CNN-based) tokenizer.\nIn input, it gets 7 tokens per frame which are decoded as a single flattened sequence. \nThis decreases the number of steps the model is required to generate. The model is able to generate tokens \ncomfortably faster than realtime playback using a straightforward vLLM implementation on an A100 or H100 \nGPU, which means longer sequences are still generated in realtime.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSNAC utilizes a hierarchy of quantizers operating at multiple temporal resolutions, allowing the codec to capture \ndetails at different time levels more efficiently.\n\nIn standard RVQ codebook operates at that same temporal resolution. \n    --> all information — from very slow-changing semantic structure to extremely fine-grained acoustic detail — \n        must be represented at the same temporal rate.\n    --> more tokens are used to represent phenomena that change very slowly.\n\nInstead of quantizing all residuals at the same frame rate, SNAC introduces a hierarchy, where each \nquantizer operates at a different temporal resolution. \n\nAt each iteration i, they downsample the residuals using average pooling , perform codebook lookup, and then upsample \nagain with nearest-neighbor interpolation by the same factor to match the original temporal resolution.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMultilingual support! Canopy Labs also released on huggingface Orpheus Multilingual, a family of speech-LLMs, for \nmultiple languages: French, German, Spanish, Italian, Chinese, Korean, and Hindi. \nThe fine tuned versions have finite set of Voices and emotion tags.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790085095077,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
