      "updated": 1790149896919,
      "link": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.01941",
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Streams Modeling",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Streams Modeling",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "created": 1790147207080,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mJPBcfI8p63eJcB2ZpkjL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6405.617518566614,
      "y": 1381.025690132392,
      "width": 926.7504882812497,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "AUB3aFUaNhb4WMMF7G_3s",
        "djdqUVVPu5OmsBe98Cob4",
        "cYYExlM5au2H5pnyc6FBm"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 703125340,
      "version": 4958,
      "versionNonce": 1415575524,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790149896919,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Instead of leaving text as is the paper stretches it across time: the aligned text stream\nuses [word] to indicate when a new word starts, and [pad] when no text symbol should\nhappen at that frame.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSo now both streams have one entry per frame. The paper also says that aligning both\ndomains to the same time grid enables batched streaming inference.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Instead of leaving text as is the paper stretches it across time: the aligned text stream uses [word] to indicate when a new word starts, and [pad] when no text symbol should happen at that frame.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSo now both streams have one entry per frame. The paper also says that aligning both domains to the same time grid enables batched streaming inference.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790147336332,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mGeDLyxo-8-0Ka1xv-N1w",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6420.585331494054,
      "y": 1954.9914257735545,
      "width": 926.7504882812497,
      "height": 1275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "erHrdWhyUQ8jymuL1RQXU",
        "kQTFSsv0maOpM5w9DlS4F",
        "TdDICc9O35ktWVsGIQelf"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9c",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 772639708,
      "version": 5189,
      "versionNonce": 81746788,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790149896919,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So now both streams have one entry per frame but alignment introduces another problem:\ncausality.\n\nWe wish to solve a sequence-to-sequence task between two domains X and Y. Each domain\nconsists of sequences of vectors of all possible lengths\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nthe task of ASR corresponds to sampling from the distribution P [Y |X], while the task of\nTTS corresponds to sampling from the distribution P [X|Y ].\n\nWe now only focus on estimating P [Y |X]. Assuming that both domains X and Y can share the\nsame time grid then one can simply model:\n\n\n\n\n\nfor this to be true, Y>t must be independent of X>t , knowing X≤t.\n\nIn words, future text tokens must be independent from future audio tokens. this is not\nalways granted!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nsimply aligning X and Y does not guarantee that streaming prediction reproduces the same\nconditional distribution as offline prediction, because future X may contain information needed\nto determine current Y.\n\nThat is why the word Delayed in DSM matters.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe condition above is achieved by delaying the output stream Yt by a number of steps τ > 0.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So now both streams have one entry per frame but alignment introduces another problem: causality.\n\nWe wish to solve a sequence-to-sequence task between two domains X and Y. Each domain consists of sequences of vectors of all possible lengths\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nthe task of ASR corresponds to sampling from the distribution P [Y |X], while the task of TTS corresponds to sampling from the distribution P [X|Y ].\n\nWe now only focus on estimating P [Y |X]. Assuming that both domains X and Y can share the same time grid then one can simply model:\n\n\n\n\n\nfor this to be true, Y>t must be independent of X>t , knowing X≤t.\n\nIn words, future text tokens must be independent from future audio tokens. this is not always granted!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nsimply aligning X and Y does not guarantee that streaming prediction reproduces the same conditional distribution as offline prediction, because future X may contain information needed to determine current Y.\n\nThat is why the word Delayed in DSM matters.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe condition above is achieved by delaying the output stream Yt by a number of steps τ > 0.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790147674280,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
