      "link": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.01941",
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Decoder-only Multimodal Models",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Decoder-only Multimodal Models",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "created": 1790146171588,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CIlM2hPTwUL8Tqxj4oaui",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4841.676103287433,
      "y": 2100.9038641307925,
      "width": 926.7504882812497,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "cTjc520rokfxnXa59u83x",
        "by3d-wLuRKRImeT4S8lkM",
        "3P28t7gPm3qCBTDhoRUyK"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bA3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1173091676,
      "version": 5101,
      "versionNonce": 1278437348,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790149896919,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The arrival of decoder-only Transformers plus discrete audio/image tokenizers made possible\nto interleave token of different nature.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBut there is a problem.\n    => Most decoder-only multimodal models use prefix conditioning\n\nThe model sees the complete input prefix first and only afterward generates the output.\n\nDecoder-only multimodal models are architecturally elegant, but their usual token\nconcatenation strategy destroys streaming.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The arrival of decoder-only Transformers plus discrete audio/image tokenizers made possible to interleave token of different nature.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBut there is a problem.\n    => Most decoder-only multimodal models use prefix conditioning\n\nThe model sees the complete input prefix first and only afterward generates the output.\n\nDecoder-only multimodal models are architecturally elegant, but their usual token concatenation strategy destroys streaming.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790146225037,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
